WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.750
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:14.550
The reading from the Sinaxadion, for October 23rd, on which we commemorate, the Holy

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:22.550
Hyromarter and Apostle James, the Brother of God.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:29.230
On the 23rd of the month, we celebrate the memory of the Holy Apostle James, the Brother

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:35.650
of the Lord, and first bishop of Jerusalem.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:41.770
St. James was born of the first marriage of Joseph, the betrothed, and was blessed by God

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.490
from his mother's womb.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:51.850
So righteous was he in his living that the Jews called him the just and the rampart

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.090
of the people.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:58.210
From childhood, he lived in the strictest abstinence.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:04.370
Like St. John the Baptist, he drank neither wine nor strong drink, and he ate no flesh

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:05.850
meat.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:12.010
All the days of his life no razor came upon his head, as the law requires in those who

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:15.850
consecrate themselves to the Lord.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:21.490
He never bathed or anointed himself with oil, since he took no thought for the body as

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:24.130
compared with the soul.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:29.250
After the Lord's ascension into heaven, the Apostles with one accord chose him to be

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.570
the first bishop of Jerusalem.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:38.810
Standing perfect and complete in all the virtues of the active and contemplative life, James

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:43.490
used to go alone into the sanctuary of the new covenant.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:50.030
Not once every year, like the high priest of the Jews, but each day, there to serve the

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.730
holy mysteries.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:02:00.050
In a garment of linen, he entered alone into the temple, and hour after hour, knelt,

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:07.090
interceding for the people, and for the salvation of the world, so that his knees became hard

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:10.090
as stone.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:16.930
St. James as chief among the Council of Elders resolved the question that had arisen in Antioch

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:23.050
about the necessity of circumcising the pagans who embraced the faith, saying that there

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:29.730
was no need to trouble them with the requirements of the old law, except that they should abstain

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:38.280
from meats offered in sacrifice to idols, and from fornication.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:43.920
St. James wrote the letter that bears his name in the canon of Scripture.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:51.000
In it, he corrects those who think God brings about the evils that befall them.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:57.000
God cannot be tempted with evil, and he tempts no one, he writes.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:06.360
But every man is tempted when he is drawn away of his own lust and enticed.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:12.720
He insists that it is not enough for someone to say he has faith in Christ because faith

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:20.240
must shine forth in virtuous deeds, for as the body without the breath is dead, so faith

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.240
without works is dead also.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:30.600
He gives a great deal of advice for leading a life acceptable to God, and for obtaining the

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:37.880
wisdom that comes from on high, teaching us to recognise the gift of God in all things.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:44.320
Very good gift, and every perfect gift, is from above, and comes down from the father

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:52.200
of lights, with whom is no veriableness, neither shadow of turning.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:59.160
He also composed the divine liturgy ascribed to him, that is the source of all the liturgies

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.320
of the Orthodox Church.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:10.120
At the year 62, when disorder and anarchy reigned in Judea, after the death of the Governor

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:18.680
Festus, the Jews foiled in their plot to put Paul to death, late hold of James, to whose

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:25.240
preaching the people gave much credence as to a just man of renown.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:31.880
Many, even among the chiefs of the people, had already embraced the faith, and the scribes

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:39.600
and Pharisees were troubled, last before long, all would recognise Jesus as Christ the

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.600
Savior.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:48.760
So, full of deceit, they approached James, praising his virtue and righteousness and said,

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:57.000
we beg you, as a just man, without partiality, urge the people who will soon be gathering here

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:06.240
for the Passover, to make no mistake about the person of Joshua, that is Jesus.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:12.440
Take up your station, therefore, on the pinnacle of the temple, from where you will be visible

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:20.600
and audible to all the people, and to the pagans that crowd in for the feast.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:25.960
When he had gone up to the highest point of the temple, the scribes and Pharisees shouted

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:34.920
up from below, O righteous and trustworthy man, tell us who this Joshua is, since the people

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:39.920
are mistakenly following Jesus who was crucified.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:49.000
Then James replied in a loud voice, why do you question me about the Son of Man?

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:55.680
He is now in heaven seated at the right hand of the mighty power, and he will come in the

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.800
clouds of heaven to judge the world in righteousness.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:09.800
The testimony of James convinced many of them, and they cried, Hosanna to the Son of David,

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:18.120
but the scribes and Pharisees gnashed their teeth at him and cried, oh, even the righteous

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:25.040
has gone astray, and they fulfilled the prophecy written by Isaiah.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:31.840
Let us do away with the righteous man, for he has become unbearable to us.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:40.020
They rushed to the pinnacle of the temple, and through St. James to the ground.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:49.620
In spite of the height, he survived the fall, and writing himself, knelt and made this prayer

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.620
to God.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:07:00.860
I beg the Lord God and Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:07.940
As he prayed thus for his tormentors, following the example of Christ and of St. Stephen,

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:11.020
the Jews stoned him.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:17.700
One of them enraged at the sight of the unshakable charity of the saint, took the club he used

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:21.980
for filling cloth and struck him on the head.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:26.820
So it was that James the just gave his testimony.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:31.780
He was buried near the temple at the place where he fell.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:38.780
The outstanding virtue of James led the more thoughtful Jews to regard his martyrdom as

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:49.100
the immediate occasion of the siege and destruction of Jerusalem in the year 70.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:56.100
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.340
and save us.
